UID:spetses-spetses-town-feast-of-the-three-spetsiot-neomartyrs-spetses--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270204
SUMMARY:Feast of the Three Spetsiot Neomartyrs\, Spetses Town
LOCATION:Spetses Town\, Spetses\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Spetses has three local saints\, the neomartyrs Nikolaos\, Ioannis and Stamatios\, martyred in Chios in 1822\, and their church in town keeps 2-3 February with vespers and an episcopal liturgy\; the 2022 bicentenary brought several bishops. A winter feast for the island's own\, not a tourist event\, but the tavernas around the Dapia are open.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#spetses-town-feast-of-the-three-spetsiot-neomartyrs-spetses-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#spetses-town-feast-of-the-three-spetsiot-neomartyrs-spetses-
END:VEVENT
